-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the automaton
-- The pattern p is the reversed end of the turn, a byte at each offset; f holds the failure of each
-- state j < m, the longest proper border of p's first j + 1 bytes, in two bytes (low first). A state is
-- how much of p is matched.
m-fail : (k : Nat) → Bytes k → Word → Word
m-fail k f j = wadd (cstr-get k f (wmul j #2)) (wmul (cstr-get k f (wadd (wmul j #2) #1)) #256)
